== S2 Liénard identity
PASS S2 (1/B) xdot = Y - F(x)  with Y = y - N(x) + F(x), N = -A/B
PASS S2 (1/B) dY/dt = -g(x)  with F' = f = N' - rho D/B, g = -rho (BC-AD)/B^2
PASS S2 f(1) = -trJ(1,1)/B(1) (uses A(1) = -B(1), i.e. (1,1) on the x-nullcline)
== S3 families 9a, 9b, 10a
PASS S3 9a: u = (q, c1*q + c3*p, p) > 0 (polynomials with positive coefficients)
PASS S3 9a: system is linear in y: A=c1*q*x**2, B=-c1*q*x - c3*p*x + c3*p
PASS S3 9a: alpha2 = alpha1 + alpha3 (alpha1 = c1u1, alpha2 = u2, alpha3 = c3u3)
PASS S3 9a: c1u1 - c3u3 = alpha1 - alpha3 = 2c1c3(-d2) - c1d3 - c3d1 (so BBH-Hopf fails <=> k = alpha3/alpha1 >= 1)
PASS S3 9a: BC - AD = u1u2u3 * x^2(1-x)
PASS S3 9a: B = alpha3 - alpha2 x, negative exactly for x > x0 = alpha3/alpha2
PASS S3 9a: on x = x0, xdot = A(x0) = alpha1 x0^2 > 0
PASS S3 9a: D(x0) = -p*q < 0 and D' = -c1*q - c3*p <= 0, hence D < 0 < -B on (x0, oo): D/B > 0
PASS S3 9a: N'(1) = (alpha1-alpha3)/alpha1 = 1-k <= 0 iff k >= 1
PASS S3 9a: D(1)/B(1) = (c1 + p)/c1 > 0, so f(1) = N'(1) - rho D(1)/B(1) < 0 when k >= 1
PASS S3 9b: u = (1, c1 + c3*d1, d1) > 0 (polynomials with positive coefficients)
PASS S3 9b: system is linear in y: A=c1*x**2, B=-c1*x - c3*d1*x + c3*d1
PASS S3 9b: alpha2 = alpha1 + alpha3 (alpha1 = c1u1, alpha2 = u2, alpha3 = c3u3)
PASS S3 9b: c1u1 - c3u3 = alpha1 - alpha3 = 2c1c3(-d2) - c1d3 - c3d1 (so BBH-Hopf fails <=> k = alpha3/alpha1 >= 1)
PASS S3 9b: BC - AD = u1u2u3 * x^2(1-x)
PASS S3 9b: B = alpha3 - alpha2 x, negative exactly for x > x0 = alpha3/alpha2
PASS S3 9b: on x = x0, xdot = A(x0) = alpha1 x0^2 > 0
PASS S3 9b: D(x0) = -d1 < 0 and D' = 0 <= 0, hence D < 0 < -B on (x0, oo): D/B > 0
PASS S3 9b: N'(1) = (alpha1-alpha3)/alpha1 = 1-k <= 0 iff k >= 1
PASS S3 9b: D(1)/B(1) = d1/c1 > 0, so f(1) = N'(1) - rho D(1)/B(1) < 0 when k >= 1
PASS S3 10a: u = (q, c1*q + c3*p, p) > 0 (polynomials with positive coefficients)
PASS S3 10a: system is linear in y: A=c1*q*x**2 + c3*p, B=-c1*q*x - c3*p*x
PASS S3 10a: alpha2 = alpha1 + alpha3 (alpha1 = c1u1, alpha2 = u2, alpha3 = c3u3)
